Strip_Trigger_Handler: uniform void(int) trigger-table signature (wasm call_indirect)

The pit/strip trigger table @0x467084 mixes handlers Ghidra typed void(int)
(PitOut/PitIn/Pit_Stop1), void(void) (Pit_Stop2) and the unexported no-op
0x448e50 (stub, now void(int) in dd2h_stubs.c); the x86 caller pushes the car
index for all of them (cdecl caller cleanup makes the arity mismatch harmless
natively), but WASM's typed call_indirect traps: "null function or function
signature mismatch" in Strip_Trigger_Handler as soon as a car crosses a pit
strip. Give Pit_Stop2 an ignored int arg and type the call through
void(*)(int) (same normalization as patches 450-480).

